      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The name Mineral Bluff was adopted in 1885, marking a new chapter for the growing settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mineral_Bluff%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Today, the town still houses the original depot, an old church, and a post office—all preserved in historic buildings.",
